1
00:02:28,415 --> 00:02:29,750
It’s crooked, it’s crooked.

2
00:02:32,953 --> 00:02:36,023
All right, all right.

3
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,226
How is it?

4
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:40,827
Good...

5
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,635
Dad, I’m off to work.

6
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:50,637
Have you tidied upstairs?

7
00:02:50,904 --> 00:02:52,172
All done.

8
00:02:53,306 --> 00:02:54,574
Off you go.

9
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:57,711
I’m leaving.

10
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,913
All right. Don’t be late coming home.

11
00:03:05,318 --> 00:03:06,586
Eldest Brother!

12
00:03:28,275 --> 00:03:30,410
- Xiaoli!
- Mom... Look what he’s doing!

13
00:03:31,144 --> 00:03:32,946
Xiaoli... Stop fooling around, okay?

14
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:35,348
Go play outside. Stop fussing.

15
00:03:41,955 --> 00:03:45,759
Look at them. The adults haven’t even met,
but the children are already friends.

16
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,229
Zengliang, come downstairs.

17
00:04:14,988 --> 00:04:19,259
A-Ju, what’s so interesting? Come back.

18
00:04:29,402 --> 00:04:31,538
Oh, it’s Mrs. Huang.
I wondered who it was.

19
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:32,606
Please come in.

20
00:04:32,873 --> 00:04:34,141
Thank you, thank you.

21
00:04:34,474 --> 00:04:36,743
Come on, we’re neighbors now.

22
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:41,148
Same profession, different branches.

23
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:44,217
Your husband practices Western medicine;
mine, Chinese.

24
00:04:44,551 --> 00:04:46,753
I hope we can learn from you someday.

25
00:04:47,687 --> 00:04:49,222
Please, don’t mention it.

26
00:04:49,489 --> 00:04:51,291
Please come in. Have a seat.

27
00:04:55,162 --> 00:04:57,898
We just moved in, so it’s all a mess.

28
00:04:58,231 --> 00:05:01,101
Second Son, this is Mrs. Huang,
Dr. Huang’s wife.

29
00:05:01,368 --> 00:05:02,969
This is our second son.

30
00:05:03,236 --> 00:05:04,704
Say hello to Auntie Huang.

31
00:05:04,905 --> 00:05:05,639
Hello, Auntie.

32
00:05:05,906 --> 00:05:07,107
You must be very busy, right?

33
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:08,575
This is my husband.

34
00:05:09,442 --> 00:05:10,911
Please sit down. Have a seat.

35
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:13,513
Second Son, go pour a cup of herbal tea.

36
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:15,048
Herbal tea?

37
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,584
We drink herbal tea all year round.

38
00:05:17,851 --> 00:05:19,386
It’s the Tai...

39
00:05:19,719 --> 00:05:23,723
It’s that Taiwanese... grass tea.

40
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:25,992
Grass tea?

41
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,728
Herbal tea.

42
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:30,330
That’s right...

43
00:05:30,463 --> 00:05:30,931
Right...

44
00:05:31,398 --> 00:05:32,866
Well, go on!

45
00:05:35,402 --> 00:05:38,138
We should have visited you first.

46
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:40,207
But instead, you came to see us.

47
00:05:40,473 --> 00:05:42,142
It was very inconsiderate of us.

48
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:44,945
Inconsiderate?

49
00:05:45,212 --> 00:05:47,280
What are you saying?

50
00:05:47,547 --> 00:05:50,417
I mean... I mean...

51
00:05:51,418 --> 00:05:54,221
We couldn’t find a maid for the move.

52
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:56,356
I’m feeling uncomfortable all over.

53
00:05:57,424 --> 00:05:58,558
It’s been hard work.

54
00:05:58,825 --> 00:05:59,893
Me?

55
00:06:06,766 --> 00:06:07,901
Thank you.

56
00:06:15,175 --> 00:06:16,776
A little bitter, isn’t it?

57
00:06:18,979 --> 00:06:20,580
No, not at all.

58
00:06:21,982 --> 00:06:25,118
Mrs. Huang,
this is my family’s secret recipe,

59
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:26,519
and it cures all diseases.

60
00:06:26,853 --> 00:06:29,789
Just gulp it down
and it won’t taste bitter.

61
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:32,459
I’ll drink it, I’ll drink it.

62
00:06:42,202 --> 00:06:43,737
It’s not bitter anymore, is it?

63
00:06:45,872 --> 00:06:47,607
Not bitter, not bitter...

64
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:59,019
Mrs. Chen,
when you said it was hard just now,

65
00:06:59,352 --> 00:07:01,354
were you talking about your husband?

66
00:07:02,689 --> 00:07:05,091
No, not him. I meant me.

67
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:07,294
I feel sore all over.

68
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,762
I’m afraid I may have arthritis.

69
00:07:09,029 --> 00:07:11,298
I’d like your husband to examine me.

70
00:07:12,966 --> 00:07:15,502
Please, don’t stand on ceremony.
Of course.

71
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:18,438
Come along. I’ll see you for free.

72
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:22,776
Mrs. Chen, I’m very afraid of injections.

73
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:27,113
I don’t trust Western medicine.
I have more faith in Chinese medicine.

74
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,648
Excellent, excellent!

75
00:07:28,982 --> 00:07:31,985
Mrs. Huang,
come see me whenever you’re ill.

76
00:07:32,319 --> 00:07:36,456
It’s free, absolutely free,
and you get a bowl of herbal tea, too.

77
00:07:40,593 --> 00:07:44,197
Mrs. Huang, please sit for a while.
I’m going upstairs to get some rest.

78
00:07:45,532 --> 00:07:48,668
If a patient comes,
come upstairs and call me.

79
00:07:52,605 --> 00:07:54,207
Mom, Dad is looking for you.

80
00:07:54,541 --> 00:07:55,942
All right. I’ll be right there.

81
00:07:56,276 --> 00:07:59,612
Mrs. Chen, do come visit me sometime.

82
00:07:59,946 --> 00:08:02,082
I’m sorry we have so little to offer you.

83
00:08:02,415 --> 00:08:04,684
Don’t mention it. I’ll be going now.

84
00:08:07,354 --> 00:08:08,955
- Goodbye.
- All right, goodbye.

85
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,163
Second Son!

86
00:08:18,698 --> 00:08:20,633
Look at you. What a hopeless case.

87
00:08:20,967 --> 00:08:23,169
You see a young lady and act like a fly.

88
00:08:23,436 --> 00:08:25,705
You nearly fell off the ladder just now.

89
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,441
What’s wrong?

90
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:30,510
I’m hurt. It aches a little.

91
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:33,446
Really?
Hurry, let your father examine you.

92
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:38,785
No. Dad’s a Chinese doctor.
Go to a Western doctor for ointment.

93
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:42,389
Big Brother is at the hospital again.

94
00:08:42,655 --> 00:08:45,058
I’ll go next door
and have them look at it.

95
00:08:46,726 --> 00:08:49,796
All right,
but don’t let your father see you.

96
00:08:52,332 --> 00:08:56,269
Hey... Don’t run! Aren’t you injured?

97
00:08:58,138 --> 00:09:00,940
Hurry and ask Dr. Huang to examine you.

98
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:07,614
Dr. Huang Hsi-ming
Office Hours
9 a.m.–noon / 2–6 p.m.
Closed Sundays
Huang Surgical Clinic

99
00:09:41,047 --> 00:09:42,248
You?

100
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:43,516
I...

101
00:09:43,850 --> 00:09:46,319
Aren’t you Dr. Chen’s son from next door?

102
00:09:47,053 --> 00:09:52,592
His son, yes. I’m Chen Zengliang.

103
00:09:52,859 --> 00:09:53,860
What’s your name?

104
00:09:54,127 --> 00:09:57,397
I... I’m A-Ju.

105
00:09:57,664 --> 00:09:58,865
A-Juan?

106
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:01,468
You came to see the doctor?

107
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:04,871
See the doctor? Yes, that’s right.

108
00:10:05,205 --> 00:10:07,474
I fell just now and got a little hurt.

109
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:10,543
I see. Sit down for a moment.

110
00:10:13,012 --> 00:10:14,814
I’ll go get the doctor.

111
00:10:15,148 --> 00:10:17,617
No, don’t call the doctor.

112
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:20,153
Just put a little medicine on it for me.

113
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:22,689
I’m not a doctor. I don’t know how.

114
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,892
I’m sure you’re even better than a doctor.

115
00:10:26,159 --> 00:10:27,961
Please take a look for me.

116
00:10:28,895 --> 00:10:30,230
All right.

117
00:10:38,238 --> 00:10:39,772
Does it hurt here?

118
00:10:41,841 --> 00:10:43,376
It hurts here.

119
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,245
I’ll rub it for you.

120
00:10:45,778 --> 00:10:48,515
All right. Thank you.

121
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,586
Your mother is so young and pretty.

122
00:10:54,721 --> 00:10:56,055
My mother?

123
00:10:57,524 --> 00:11:01,461
No, no, not my mother. She’s my second...

124
00:11:01,728 --> 00:11:07,133
No, she’s my... my after-mother.

125
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,334
What?

126
00:11:08,535 --> 00:11:10,136
After-mother.

127
00:11:11,204 --> 00:11:12,005
Stepmother.

128
00:11:12,272 --> 00:11:14,941
That’s right, my stepmother.
My stepmother.

129
00:11:19,946 --> 00:11:23,283
I can’t take it anymore.
I surrender, A-Ju!

130
00:11:25,218 --> 00:11:26,486
You’re so kind.

131
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:28,621
Thank you.

132
00:11:36,896 --> 00:11:39,632
Shame on you! Shameless!

133
00:11:39,899 --> 00:11:42,502
Get out... Get out!

134
00:11:50,577 --> 00:11:51,711
Who are you looking for?

135
00:11:51,978 --> 00:11:53,513
Are you hiring someone here?

136
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:54,847
I don’t know.

137
00:11:56,849 --> 00:11:57,850
Who are you looking for?

138
00:11:58,184 --> 00:12:00,853
Madam, is this the Chen residence?

139
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,855
The employment agency sent me.

140
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:05,458
All right, come in.

141
00:12:09,062 --> 00:12:10,330
Is there a patient?

142
00:12:21,608 --> 00:12:23,209
Auntie Huang.

143
00:12:23,476 --> 00:12:25,678
Aren’t you Dr. Chen’s second son?

144
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:30,817
Yes...
I took a fall and got a little hurt.

145
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:34,754
Have the doctor examine you right away.

146
00:12:35,154 --> 00:12:39,959
Dr. Huang, this is Dr. Chen's second son
from next door.

147
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:43,830
Very good, very good. Let me take a look.

148
00:12:45,164 --> 00:12:47,567
No need. A-Ju has already examined me.

149
00:12:47,834 --> 00:12:49,302
Her? What does she know?

150
00:12:49,569 --> 00:12:51,704
Come on... Let me take a look.

151
00:12:51,971 --> 00:12:53,840
Me? All right, come here.

152
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,116
I’m fine now. It doesn’t hurt.

153
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:05,184
Take it off.

154
00:13:05,918 --> 00:13:06,919
It doesn’t hurt anymore.

155
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,522
Take off your shirt.

156
00:13:10,723 --> 00:13:11,991
What?

157
00:13:12,258 --> 00:13:13,393
Take it off.

158
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,529
- Take off your clothes.
- Yes.

159
00:13:40,687 --> 00:13:41,888
Does it hurt here?

160
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:45,224
It hurts here! It hurts here!

161
00:13:51,964 --> 00:13:52,832
All right.

162
00:13:57,904 --> 00:13:59,706
It’s a little swollen.

163
00:13:59,972 --> 00:14:02,108
I’ll give you an injection.

164
00:14:05,111 --> 00:14:06,179
A shot.

165
00:14:10,049 --> 00:14:11,050
An injection?

166
00:15:14,514 --> 00:15:15,515
There, all done.

167
00:15:23,122 --> 00:15:25,925
Thank you, thank you.

168
00:15:27,326 --> 00:15:28,461
How much is it?

169
00:15:28,728 --> 00:15:32,331
Nothing. We’re neighbors. It’s free.

170
00:15:33,666 --> 00:15:35,935
Thank you, thank you.

171
00:15:36,402 --> 00:15:38,137
Does it still hurt?

172
00:15:38,404 --> 00:15:40,006
It hurts...

173
00:15:40,473 --> 00:15:42,074
It still hurts?

174
00:15:42,341 --> 00:15:44,076
N-no... It doesn’t hurt at all.

175
00:15:46,078 --> 00:15:48,881
Come back tomorrow for another shot.

176
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:54,153
Tomorrow?

177
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:56,022
All right, all right.

178
00:16:09,435 --> 00:16:12,371
That’ll teach him a lesson.

179
00:16:17,243 --> 00:16:22,582
A-Ju, don’t forget:
I’m the one who raised you.

180
00:16:22,849 --> 00:16:25,651
One day, you’ll be my daughter-in-law.

181
00:16:28,521 --> 00:16:32,124
I just got a letter from Wuxiong.

182
00:16:32,391 --> 00:16:35,461
He’ll be discharged in a day or two.

183
00:16:35,728 --> 00:16:39,332
When he’s back, we’ll let them marry.

184
00:16:50,743 --> 00:16:51,878
Cousin!

185
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,216
Sorry to keep you waiting.

186
00:16:57,483 --> 00:16:59,685
Cousin, why are you being so formal?

187
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:02,622
People say I, Liang Peiyun,
am chasing you.

188
00:17:02,955 --> 00:17:04,957
Cousin,
there you go making things up again.

189
00:17:05,224 --> 00:17:06,893
Then you have to take me out.

190
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:09,095
All right. Wait until I get off work.

191
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:21,774
Cousin,
this classmate studied civil engineering.

192
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:24,310
He’ll be discharged in a day or two.

193
00:17:24,644 --> 00:17:25,912
I’ll need your help then

194
00:17:26,245 --> 00:17:28,447
and get him a job
at Uncle’s construction firm.

195
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,316
I know, I know.

196
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:32,985
You only talk about others. What a bore.

197
00:17:33,586 --> 00:17:35,922
Cousin, seriously,

198
00:17:36,255 --> 00:17:38,524
my classmate is quite handsome.

199
00:17:38,858 --> 00:17:40,726
I'm sure you'll like him when you meet.

200
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,066
Meizhi!

201
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,072
Peiyun, you’re here too.

202
00:17:53,339 --> 00:17:54,340
Just the two of you?

203
00:17:54,607 --> 00:17:55,675
Why don’t you join us?

204
00:17:55,942 --> 00:17:56,475
No, thanks.

205
00:17:56,809 --> 00:17:58,344
We have friends coming shortly.

206
00:17:58,544 --> 00:17:59,545
See you later.

207
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:01,414
I forgot to introduce you.

208
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:03,883
This is my classmate, Miss Huang Meizhi.
Miss Huang,

209
00:18:04,216 --> 00:18:06,953
this is my cousin, Mr. Chen Zenghong.

210
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:09,889
Mr. Chen.

211
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:14,961
Miss Huang, please sit for a while.

212
00:18:15,227 --> 00:18:17,029
No, thank you.

213
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:18,230
Goodbye.

214
00:18:40,586 --> 00:18:42,588
Cousin, do you like her?

215
00:18:42,922 --> 00:18:46,459
I like her. I like her...

216
00:19:05,277 --> 00:19:06,612
A-Ju!

217
00:19:09,682 --> 00:19:11,217
- I’m leaving.
- All right.

218
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:23,362
Good morning, Miss Huang.

219
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,899
Good morning, Mr. Chen.

220
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:32,238
Miss Huang, do you live around here too?

221
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:33,572
Yes, I do.

222
00:19:38,244 --> 00:19:39,245
Second Son!

223
00:19:40,246 --> 00:19:41,380
Good morning, Mom.

224
00:19:41,714 --> 00:19:45,317
Good morning. Moving these past few days
has left my back aching all over.

225
00:19:45,651 --> 00:19:47,720
I’m thinking of going out to see a doctor.

226
00:19:47,987 --> 00:19:49,455
Why not let Dad examine you?

227
00:19:49,789 --> 00:19:51,724
Him? I don’t trust him.

228
00:19:52,925 --> 00:19:54,527
Then let me take a look.

229
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,196
I know how much you know about medicine.

230
00:19:58,531 --> 00:19:59,865
Then go to the neighbors.

231
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,003
Just don’t let your father hear.

232
00:20:11,277 --> 00:20:13,212
A-Ju, is Dr. Huang in?

233
00:20:13,412 --> 00:20:14,613
Yes, he is.

234
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:18,150
Dr. Huang!

235
00:20:18,484 --> 00:20:20,086
Mrs. Chen, what can I do for you?

236
00:20:20,352 --> 00:20:21,887
Please, come in.

237
00:20:22,154 --> 00:20:23,022
All right.

238
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:31,964
Dr. Huang, I’d like you to examine me.

239
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:33,432
An examination?

240
00:20:33,699 --> 00:20:35,501
I ache all over.

241
00:20:35,835 --> 00:20:37,770
What about Dr. Chen, your husband?

242
00:20:38,104 --> 00:20:39,572
Him? I don’t trust him.

243
00:20:39,839 --> 00:20:41,307
I believe in Western medicine.

244
00:20:42,374 --> 00:20:44,043
My own wife doesn’t trust me either.

245
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:46,445
She prefers your herbal tea.

246
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,647
I see.

247
00:20:48,981 --> 00:20:51,317
- Let me examine you. Please sit down.
- All right.

248
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:56,589
Does it hurt here?

249
00:20:58,991 --> 00:21:02,128
Turn around a little. Turn around.

250
00:21:02,328 --> 00:21:03,195
All right.

251
00:21:06,532 --> 00:21:08,000
Does it hurt here?

252
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,668
No, it doesn’t hurt here.

253
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:11,203
What about here?

254
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:12,805
A little lower.

255
00:21:13,072 --> 00:21:14,206
Here...

256
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,610
I’m sorry...

257
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:19,612
What about here?

258
00:21:22,348 --> 00:21:23,415
Does it hurt here?

259
00:21:23,682 --> 00:21:24,483
Here.

260
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:25,684
What about this side?

261
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:27,353
Pardon me, pardon me.

262
00:21:29,755 --> 00:21:30,756
And over here?

263
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,691
- Here.
- It doesn’t hurt there.

264
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:34,026
Come over this way.

265
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:37,029
Turn around.

266
00:21:38,164 --> 00:21:39,832
Let me have a look at your foot.

267
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:51,977
It’s fine, it’s fine.

268
00:21:52,244 --> 00:21:54,046
I’ll give you an injection.

269
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,656
What are you laughing at? What’s so funny?

270
00:22:03,923 --> 00:22:06,258
You little brat! Come on!

271
00:22:20,139 --> 00:22:22,808
Mrs. Huang, I came to see Dr. Huang.

272
00:22:23,742 --> 00:22:25,144
How much do I owe you?

273
00:22:25,411 --> 00:22:26,212
Nothing.

274
00:22:26,879 --> 00:22:28,414
Oh, I couldn’t possibly accept that.

275
00:22:28,681 --> 00:22:30,015
No, please, don’t mention it.

276
00:22:30,883 --> 00:22:32,685
All right, thank you.

277
00:22:32,885 --> 00:22:33,886
Goodbye.

278
00:22:38,757 --> 00:22:40,492
A medical consultation, huh?

279
00:22:41,227 --> 00:22:44,630
Who’d believe that?
Do you think I’m an idiot?

280
00:22:45,231 --> 00:22:47,099
You’re suspicious of me again.

281
00:22:47,433 --> 00:22:51,971
I know Mrs. Chen is young and pretty,

282
00:22:52,238 --> 00:22:53,706
but don’t get any ideas.

283
00:22:55,241 --> 00:23:00,312
Madam, I wouldn’t. Don’t worry.

284
00:23:00,579 --> 00:23:02,715
I was only examining her, after all.

285
00:23:02,982 --> 00:23:05,317
Examining her?
Don’t you ever examine her again.

286
00:23:12,658 --> 00:23:13,726
Brother Wuxiong!

287
00:23:14,593 --> 00:23:15,728
A-Ju!

288
00:23:15,995 --> 00:23:16,996
You’re back!

289
00:23:18,530 --> 00:23:20,599
You’ve grown up.

290
00:23:20,866 --> 00:23:21,533
Are they home?

291
00:23:21,734 --> 00:23:22,868
Yes, they are.

292
00:23:23,202 --> 00:23:26,005
Dad! Mom! Brother Wuxiong is back!

293
00:23:26,272 --> 00:23:27,206
Dad!

294
00:23:28,007 --> 00:23:29,275
Mom!

295
00:23:33,545 --> 00:23:36,282
Mom, you look very healthy.

296
00:23:36,548 --> 00:23:38,617
You... you’ve become so handsome.

297
00:23:40,019 --> 00:23:42,021
But your skin’s gotten darker.

298
00:23:47,359 --> 00:23:49,028
Dad, Mom,

299
00:23:49,361 --> 00:23:51,163
I brought you both some gifts.

300
00:24:11,717 --> 00:24:13,652
Mom, this one is for you.

301
00:24:15,921 --> 00:24:17,790
Dad, this one is for you.

302
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:26,131
- Dr. Huang!
- A-Ju!

303
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,133
I bought you some fabric. Do you like it?

304
00:24:28,467 --> 00:24:29,401
Is your hand better?

305
00:24:29,668 --> 00:24:31,003
Much better.

306
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:32,671
Let me change your dressing.

307
00:24:38,744 --> 00:24:41,613
Mom, is Meizhi still working at the co-op?

308
00:24:41,814 --> 00:24:42,481
Yes.

309
00:24:42,815 --> 00:24:44,750
I bought her a dress. Please put it away.

310
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,553
It’s a dress.

311
00:24:54,693 --> 00:24:56,028
Where’s Xiaolong?

312
00:24:56,362 --> 00:24:57,963
He’s upstairs. I’ll take you to him.

313
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:01,767
Mom, I’ll go upstairs for a moment.

314
00:25:02,034 --> 00:25:02,968
All right.

315
00:25:15,314 --> 00:25:16,315
- Xiaolong!
- Sis!

316
00:25:16,582 --> 00:25:18,517
- Xiaolong!
- Brother, you’re back!

317
00:25:18,851 --> 00:25:20,586
I bought you this model plane.
Do you like it?

318
00:25:20,853 --> 00:25:21,854
I’m so happy!

319
00:25:22,721 --> 00:25:26,191
- Let me play with it!
- Give it back to me...

320
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:34,133
Look.

321
00:25:35,134 --> 00:25:37,002
You haven’t practiced lately, have you?

322
00:25:52,885 --> 00:25:53,352
Two.

323
00:25:53,619 --> 00:25:55,421
Three.

324
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:03,762
You’ve gotten heavier.

325
00:26:05,964 --> 00:26:08,167
A-Ju, I'm sorry you worked so hard
while I was away.

326
00:26:08,434 --> 00:26:09,435
Not at all.

327
00:26:15,841 --> 00:26:17,976
Well, this move turned out great.

328
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:20,179
All the patients moved away with us!

329
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:26,452
A-Ju, I’m going to see a friend.

330
00:26:26,785 --> 00:26:28,587
You just got back.
Why don’t you rest first?

331
00:26:28,854 --> 00:26:29,855
Is it that urgent?

332
00:26:30,189 --> 00:26:31,723
He’s nearby. I’ll be right back.

333
00:26:31,924 --> 00:26:32,925
All right.

334
00:26:35,994 --> 00:26:37,463
Excuse me...

335
00:26:37,729 --> 00:26:38,797
Are you...?

336
00:26:39,131 --> 00:26:40,799
I’m here to see Dr. Chen.

337
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:45,537
You want to see the Chinese doctor...

338
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,875
Please, sit inside.

339
00:26:50,142 --> 00:26:51,143
Come in and have a seat.

340
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,083
Dear, pour a cup of herbal tea.

341
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,151
All right.

342
00:27:01,487 --> 00:27:03,222
- Sit here.
- Thank you.

343
00:27:12,831 --> 00:27:13,899
I...

344
00:27:16,101 --> 00:27:17,302
Have some herbal tea.

345
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:27,779
Sir, what seems to be the trouble?

346
00:27:28,046 --> 00:27:30,382
- I’m not sick.
- You’re not sick?

347
00:27:30,716 --> 00:27:32,384
Then what are you doing here?

348
00:27:32,651 --> 00:27:34,386
I’m here to see someone.

349
00:27:34,386 --> 00:27:37,559
Graduate, Department of Civil
Engineering
Huang Wuxiong
Taipei, Taiwan

350
00:27:38,190 --> 00:27:39,591
He’s an old classmate of mine.

351
00:27:39,858 --> 00:27:41,126
Miss Meng, where is he?

352
00:27:41,393 --> 00:27:42,728
He’s waiting in the corridor.

353
00:27:42,995 --> 00:27:44,263
Thank you.

354
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:52,404
- Wuxiong!
- Zenghong!

355
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:54,206
- Long time no see!
- Yes...

356
00:27:55,941 --> 00:27:57,009
You look better than ever.

357
00:27:57,276 --> 00:27:58,410
Oh, not at all. How are you?

358
00:27:59,878 --> 00:28:01,880
I went by your house to find you.

359
00:28:02,147 --> 00:28:03,682
Your father thought I was a patient.

360
00:28:04,016 --> 00:28:06,084
Did he give you a cup of herbal tea?

361
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:09,221
He did... It was so bitter.

362
00:28:10,088 --> 00:28:12,558
My father loves giving out herbal tea.

363
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,694
The old gentleman is quite a character.

364
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:20,165
Wuxiong, I’ve arranged a job for you.

365
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:22,301
At my uncle’s construction company.

366
00:28:22,634 --> 00:28:24,970
I’ll introduce you to my cousin.

367
00:28:25,237 --> 00:28:25,971
Do your best.

368
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:28,840
You could get a job
and a girlfriend at once.

369
00:28:29,641 --> 00:28:32,511
Don’t joke. Your cousin likes you.

370
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,247
I can’t handle her temper.

371
00:28:35,514 --> 00:28:37,716
Personally,
I prefer local Taiwanese girls.

372
00:28:37,983 --> 00:28:40,519
Taiwanese girls are sweet and gentle.

373
00:28:40,786 --> 00:28:42,387
I prefer Mainlander girls.

374
00:28:42,654 --> 00:28:44,990
Mainlander girls are more exciting.

375
00:28:45,257 --> 00:28:46,592
So you’re looking for excitement?

376
00:28:48,527 --> 00:28:51,597
Zenghong,
if you like local Taiwanese girls,

377
00:28:51,863 --> 00:28:52,998
I can introduce you to my sister.

378
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,801
Really?
Dr. Chen, the chief wants to see you.

379
00:28:56,068 --> 00:28:57,002
All right, I’ll go now.

380
00:28:57,336 --> 00:28:59,004
Zenghong, get back to work. I’ll go.

381
00:28:59,338 --> 00:29:01,673
Don’t rush off.
I’ll treat you to dinner tonight

382
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:02,741
to welcome you back.

383
00:29:03,008 --> 00:29:04,476
You don’t have to do that.

384
00:29:17,889 --> 00:29:19,024
Excuse me! Pardon me!

385
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:23,161
What’s the matter with you?
Don’t you watch where you’re going?

386
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:25,897
Miss, I hope I didn’t hurt you.

387
00:29:27,566 --> 00:29:28,900
I’m terribly sorry.

388
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:31,436
Please don’t be angry.

389
00:30:37,235 --> 00:30:37,903
Zenghong!

390
00:30:38,236 --> 00:30:39,838
Wuxiong, I’m sorry. I’m so sorry.

391
00:30:40,105 --> 00:30:40,772
Sorry I’m late.

392
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:42,374
Not at all, Cousin.

393
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:44,509
Come...

394
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:47,045
Let me introduce you.

395
00:30:47,312 --> 00:30:49,648
This is my cousin, Miss Liang Peiyun.

396
00:30:49,981 --> 00:30:52,384
This is my classmate, Huang Wuxiong.

397
00:30:56,321 --> 00:30:59,591
I never expected you to be Miss Liang.

398
00:31:00,659 --> 00:31:02,394
What? Do you two know each other?

399
00:31:03,662 --> 00:31:05,063
Yes, yes, we’ve met.

400
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:21,346
Miss Liang...

401
00:31:21,613 --> 00:31:23,548
Why don’t you call me Peiyun?

402
00:31:25,150 --> 00:31:29,554
Pe... Peiyun.
I’ll get a car to take you home.

403
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:32,157
What? You don’t want to walk with me?

404
00:31:33,158 --> 00:31:33,759
No...

405
00:31:34,092 --> 00:31:36,294
I’m afraid you’ll get home too late.

406
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:39,097
It’s all right, Wuxiong.

407
00:32:06,725 --> 00:32:08,527
My father hasn’t come yet?

408
00:32:08,727 --> 00:32:09,995
No, he hasn’t.

409
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:11,596
Wuxiong, let’s go.

410
00:32:11,863 --> 00:32:13,131
You can start work another day.

411
00:32:13,465 --> 00:32:15,467
All right. I’ll be going, then.

412
00:32:17,392 --> 00:32:21,273
Taipei District Consumers’ Cooperative

413
00:32:25,877 --> 00:32:26,878
Miss Huang!

414
00:32:28,013 --> 00:32:29,147
Mr. Chen!

415
00:32:32,284 --> 00:32:33,485
Miss Huang!

416
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:36,288
Meizhi, I’d better get going.

417
00:32:36,555 --> 00:32:38,356
Wait a moment...

418
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:39,691
Why are you like this?

419
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:45,230
Miss Huang, let me take you out to dinner.

420
00:32:48,366 --> 00:32:50,569
How did you know I worked here?

421
00:32:51,369 --> 00:32:53,104
My cousin told me.

422
00:32:53,839 --> 00:32:55,307
If your cousin knew you came to see me,

423
00:32:55,574 --> 00:32:57,175
she’d be furious.

424
00:32:58,043 --> 00:33:01,246
She won’t. I found her a boyfriend.

425
00:33:01,513 --> 00:33:03,114
He studied civil engineering.

426
00:33:04,316 --> 00:33:06,585
You’re certainly generous.

427
00:33:09,387 --> 00:33:10,655
Let’s go.

428
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,013
A-Ju!

429
00:33:36,281 --> 00:33:39,818
Shall I take you to the children’s park?

430
00:33:40,085 --> 00:33:42,487
What... what do you mean, “children”?

431
00:33:43,221 --> 00:33:48,026
The children’s park...
It’s next to the zoo,

432
00:33:49,628 --> 00:33:52,430
the zoo with the tigers and lions.

433
00:33:53,365 --> 00:33:54,766
I don’t know.

434
00:33:55,567 --> 00:33:58,370
Do you really not understand,
or are you pretending not to?

435
00:33:58,637 --> 00:34:01,172
- A-Ju!
- Coming!

436
00:34:02,107 --> 00:34:03,642
I don’t understand!

437
00:34:10,382 --> 00:34:11,783
I don’t understand.

438
00:34:12,450 --> 00:34:14,586
I don’t understand...

439
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:22,193
That’s close enough.

440
00:34:23,328 --> 00:34:25,263
How do you say, “You’re so pretty”?

441
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:27,065
Pay me a dollar first.

442
00:34:29,534 --> 00:34:32,470
- You’re beautiful.
- You’re beautiful.

443
00:34:32,747 --> 00:34:36,608
- You’re beautiful.
- You’re beautiful.

444
00:34:40,211 --> 00:34:43,615
How do you say, “Let’s go out Sunday”?

445
00:34:43,882 --> 00:34:45,283
That’ll cost you two dollars.

446
00:34:45,550 --> 00:34:47,419
Why did the price go up so quickly?

447
00:34:48,286 --> 00:34:50,088
All right... Here are two dollars.

448
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:55,894
“Let’s go out together on Sunday, okay?”

449
00:34:56,227 --> 00:34:59,230
“Sunday... us... go...
get a haircut, okay?”

450
00:34:59,564 --> 00:35:03,034
“Let’s go out together on Sunday, okay?”

451
00:35:03,368 --> 00:35:07,706
“Sunday... us... go...
get a haircut, okay?”

452
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:09,841
You really... Forget it, forget it.

453
00:35:11,309 --> 00:35:16,514
“Sunday... us... go...
get a haircut, okay?”

454
00:35:17,849 --> 00:35:20,986
Xiaoli, teach me one more phrase. I...

455
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:25,790
How do you say, “I love you”?

456
00:35:26,057 --> 00:35:27,192
Big Brother, what are you doing?

457
00:35:27,459 --> 00:35:29,060
I’m going to tell Dad!

458
00:35:30,061 --> 00:35:31,262
Don’t!

459
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:34,466
That phrase will cost you five dollars.

460
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:35,934
Five dollars?

461
00:35:36,201 --> 00:35:37,535
Take it or leave it.

462
00:35:39,604 --> 00:35:40,271
All right...

463
00:35:44,476 --> 00:35:46,011
You really know how to fleece me.

464
00:35:46,344 --> 00:35:48,813
Here’s a dollar. Teach me another phrase.

465
00:35:49,080 --> 00:35:50,215
What do you want to learn?

466
00:35:50,482 --> 00:35:53,618
Teach me... children...

467
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:56,021
- Children’s Day?
- No.

468
00:35:56,554 --> 00:35:58,890
Children’s... children’s hospital?

469
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:00,025
No.

470
00:36:00,358 --> 00:36:03,161
- Children’s amusement park?
- Yes... children’s amusement park.

471
00:36:03,428 --> 00:36:06,765
No, no. Children’s amusement park.

472
00:36:07,032 --> 00:36:09,501
Children’s amusement park.

473
00:36:09,768 --> 00:36:12,437
Children’s amusement park.

474
00:36:12,704 --> 00:36:15,240
Children’s amusement park.

475
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:16,508
Close enough.

476
00:36:16,775 --> 00:36:19,044
Children’s amusement park.

477
00:36:19,377 --> 00:36:20,578
What else do you want to learn?

478
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:23,181
Children’s amusement park.

479
00:36:24,249 --> 00:36:25,450
Now teach me...

480
00:36:25,784 --> 00:36:27,786
How do you say, “I promise you”?

481
00:36:28,053 --> 00:36:30,789
I promise you.

482
00:36:31,093 --> 00:36:33,324
I promise you.

483
00:36:34,125 --> 00:36:36,528
I promise you.

484
00:36:36,812 --> 00:36:39,264
I promise you.

485
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:41,933
I promise you.

486
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:44,335
I promise you.

487
00:36:44,602 --> 00:36:45,937
That’s right...

488
00:36:46,337 --> 00:36:48,540
Now teach me something insulting.

489
00:36:51,476 --> 00:36:53,011
Let me think.

490
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:58,683
You old devil!

491
00:36:58,950 --> 00:37:02,287
You old devil!

492
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:05,490
You old devil! You old devil!

493
00:37:06,491 --> 00:37:08,493
Not bad. All right...

494
00:37:41,126 --> 00:37:47,465
Number 27... Number 27!

495
00:37:49,334 --> 00:37:53,071
You old devil!

496
00:38:36,114 --> 00:38:39,184
I told you not to drink,
but you went and drank again.

497
00:38:39,784 --> 00:38:41,452
Why won’t you listen to me?

498
00:38:43,188 --> 00:38:45,456
Keep this up and you’ll be dead and gone.

499
00:38:46,257 --> 00:38:48,593
What? Dead uncle?

500
00:38:48,927 --> 00:38:53,798
No, “dead and gone” just means you’ll die.

501
00:38:55,066 --> 00:38:57,001
Mainlanders say this to mean
'you're finished.'

502
00:38:57,268 --> 00:38:59,003
Is it really that serious?

503
00:38:59,537 --> 00:39:03,007
You can’t have alcohol in your liver.

504
00:39:03,274 --> 00:39:05,677
- Understand?
- I understand...

505
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:11,816
You drink so much...

506
00:39:12,150 --> 00:39:14,018
If you won’t listen to me,

507
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:16,221
then go find another doctor.

508
00:39:16,821 --> 00:39:19,490
Then can I see a Chinese medicine doctor?

509
00:39:19,757 --> 00:39:21,426
That’s up to you.

510
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:24,362
Then I'll see a Chinese medicine doctor.

511
00:39:28,967 --> 00:39:31,903
A-Zhu, go make some tea.

512
00:39:32,170 --> 00:39:34,172
I'm still cleaning the tables and chairs.

513
00:39:35,240 --> 00:39:36,841
The master is downstairs seeing a patient.

514
00:39:37,108 --> 00:39:37,909
Go pour the tea first.

515
00:39:38,176 --> 00:39:40,311
You can do the other chores afterward.

516
00:39:40,578 --> 00:39:42,513
What do you mean, “other chores”?

517
00:39:43,982 --> 00:39:47,785
Other chores: wiping tables and chairs.

518
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:52,257
Wiping the tables and chairs
is “other chores”?

519
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:56,127
A-Ju, you really need to learn Mandarin.

520
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:58,196
You want me to learn Mandarin?

521
00:39:58,529 --> 00:40:00,131
All right, all right.
Go pour the tea first.

522
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:01,466
All right.

523
00:40:11,943 --> 00:40:15,280
Xiting, we’ve only just moved here.

524
00:40:15,546 --> 00:40:17,548
People don’t know your reputation yet.

525
00:40:17,882 --> 00:40:20,618
Look how busy the clinic next door is.

526
00:40:20,885 --> 00:40:22,420
How many times have I told you?

527
00:40:22,754 --> 00:40:24,555
A doctor's job is to save lives
and help people,

528
00:40:24,822 --> 00:40:26,824
not to make money.

529
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:29,027
How can you call it a business? Honestly!

530
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:30,962
Then what would you call it?

531
00:40:36,768 --> 00:40:39,170
I think we should hold a free clinic.

532
00:40:39,504 --> 00:40:41,639
That'll draw patients from next door.

533
00:40:42,373 --> 00:40:46,311
I'm all for free consultations,
but not stealing their patients.

534
00:40:46,644 --> 00:40:50,581
That settles it. Starting tomorrow,
we’ll offer free consultations.

535
00:40:50,581 --> 00:40:54,919
Dr. Chen Xiting
Grand Opening: Seven Days of Free
Consultations

536
00:41:10,268 --> 00:41:13,938
Ladies and gentlemen,
these Health and Vitality Pills

537
00:41:14,272 --> 00:41:17,342
These tonic pills use our secret recipe:
certified, effective, and a cure-all.

538
00:41:17,742 --> 00:41:20,078
Headaches, stomachaches, colds,
flu, backaches and sore shoulders...

539
00:41:20,345 --> 00:41:22,280
One bottle brings relief; two cure you.

540
00:41:22,613 --> 00:41:24,949
Please recommend them to your friends.
Thank you!

541
00:41:25,283 --> 00:41:27,151
Here, I’ll give you a bottle for free.

542
00:41:27,418 --> 00:41:28,753
Give me a bottle...

543
00:41:29,020 --> 00:41:31,422
All right... Here’s a bottle for you.

544
00:41:31,689 --> 00:41:32,824
There you go...

545
00:41:39,230 --> 00:41:44,369
A-Ju, business is looking good today.

546
00:41:44,569 --> 00:41:46,104
Everybody hates you.

547
00:41:46,310 --> 00:41:47,238
What?

548
00:41:48,792 --> 00:41:50,683
Pardon me, pardon me.

549
00:41:50,975 --> 00:41:53,280
You old devil!

550
00:42:05,456 --> 00:42:06,924
Did you see that?

551
00:42:07,258 --> 00:42:08,993
The clinic next door says
consultations are free.

552
00:42:09,327 --> 00:42:11,929
They’re stealing all the patients,
one by one.

553
00:42:12,997 --> 00:42:15,133
Seeing patients isn’t running a business.

554
00:42:16,334 --> 00:42:19,337
Then that means working for nothing.

555
00:42:20,671 --> 00:42:24,542
A doctor should help people, save lives,
not make money.

556
00:42:24,809 --> 00:42:26,144
I don’t want to hear it.

557
00:42:26,411 --> 00:42:29,747
Making money comes first;
saving lives comes second.

558
00:42:37,955 --> 00:42:38,890
A-Ju!

559
00:42:41,292 --> 00:42:44,228
I’m going to lie down for a while.
Call me if a patient comes.

560
00:42:44,495 --> 00:42:45,563
All right.

561
00:42:50,435 --> 00:42:52,437
Number 51, number 52!

562
00:42:56,974 --> 00:42:58,910
Numbers 53 and 54, numbers 55 and 56!

563
00:42:59,243 --> 00:43:01,913
57, 58, 59, 60!

564
00:44:17,455 --> 00:44:18,389
Thank you, thank you.

565
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:20,725
Thank you.

566
00:44:20,992 --> 00:44:22,126
Thank you, thank you.

567
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:25,396
- Thank you, thank you.
- Thank you.

568
00:44:25,596 --> 00:44:26,664
Thank you.

569
00:44:28,065 --> 00:44:29,267
Thank...

570
00:44:29,667 --> 00:44:32,870
Dear, I’m exhausted.

571
00:44:33,204 --> 00:44:36,674
Second Son, help your father upstairs
so he can rest.

572
00:45:05,636 --> 00:45:07,572
Mrs. Huang, please sit down.

573
00:45:08,439 --> 00:45:10,641
Business seems to be good today.

574
00:45:10,908 --> 00:45:11,842
Business?

575
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:14,445
These days, as long as something is free,

576
00:45:14,712 --> 00:45:16,581
People want a bargain,
even at the doctor’s.

577
00:45:16,847 --> 00:45:17,848
Yes... Please sit down.

578
00:45:18,983 --> 00:45:22,453
By the way, Mrs. Huang, here's a bottle
of my Health and Vitality Pills.

579
00:45:22,853 --> 00:45:25,122
My family’s secret recipe,
officially tested and highly effective.

580
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:26,390
They cure everything.

581
00:45:26,791 --> 00:45:29,060
Headaches, stomachaches, colds,
flu, backaches and sore shoulders...

582
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:30,995
One bottle helps; two cure you.

583
00:45:31,262 --> 00:45:33,464
Please recommend them to others.
Thank you.

584
00:45:33,798 --> 00:45:35,800
Try a bottle. It’s a free gift.

585
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:37,335
It won’t cost you anything.

586
00:45:38,469 --> 00:45:39,670
Nothing at all.

587
00:45:41,005 --> 00:45:43,608
And how much does a jar
like this sell for?

588
00:45:43,941 --> 00:45:45,876
It’s very cheap.
Forty dollars, with 20 percent off.

589
00:45:46,143 --> 00:45:47,878
That’s only thirty-two dollars.

590
00:45:48,879 --> 00:45:51,749
I see. Well,
I wouldn’t want to refuse your kindness.

591
00:45:51,949 --> 00:45:52,750
Thank you.

592
00:45:53,084 --> 00:45:55,686
Don’t mention it.
Come, sit down for a while.

593
00:45:56,687 --> 00:45:58,556
All right.

594
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,024
Mom!

595
00:46:00,891 --> 00:46:02,159
Auntie Huang!

596
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:05,096
Dad’s worked himself sick.

597
00:46:06,163 --> 00:46:08,432
What are we going to do about
the afternoon consultations?

598
00:46:08,766 --> 00:46:12,036
Don’t worry. I’ll fill in for him.

599
00:46:37,061 --> 00:46:39,263
I can’t let A-Ju down.

600
00:46:39,530 --> 00:46:41,399
I can’t steal their patients.

601
00:46:53,010 --> 00:46:54,612
Have some herbal tea first.

602
00:47:20,104 --> 00:47:21,505
What’s wrong with you?

603
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:25,643
It hurts here. I have a liver ailment.

604
00:47:28,179 --> 00:47:30,047
Have you seen a doctor before?

605
00:47:31,048 --> 00:47:32,850
Yes, a Western doctor.

606
00:47:33,784 --> 00:47:35,586
I believe in Chinese medicine.

607
00:48:08,686 --> 00:48:10,554
Why are you using so much
force to examine me?

608
00:48:12,690 --> 00:48:14,625
Just because I'm sick
doesn't mean you can arm-wrestle me!

609
00:48:14,892 --> 00:48:16,560
All right. Let’s see who wins.

610
00:49:37,041 --> 00:49:38,175
How is it?

611
00:49:38,442 --> 00:49:40,244
I give up! I give up!

612
00:49:40,578 --> 00:49:42,980
Then go next door
and get an injection from Dr. Huang.

613
00:49:44,181 --> 00:49:45,716
Don’t I need to take Chinese medicine?

614
00:49:45,983 --> 00:49:47,518
One injection and you’ll be better.

615
00:49:47,785 --> 00:49:49,186
My illness isn’t serious.

616
00:49:49,453 --> 00:49:51,589
It’s all right. Hurry, go on.

617
00:49:52,456 --> 00:49:55,059
All right. Thank you, thank you.

618
00:50:20,751 --> 00:50:23,153
Go next door
and get an injection from Dr. Huang.

619
00:50:23,354 --> 00:50:24,288
Get an injection.

620
00:50:24,555 --> 00:50:26,423
The injection will make you better.

621
00:50:31,028 --> 00:50:32,696
Go next door
and get an injection from Dr. Huang.

622
00:50:32,963 --> 00:50:33,831
Go get a shot!

623
00:50:36,700 --> 00:50:39,503
All of you,
go next door and get injections!

624
00:50:56,987 --> 00:50:57,855
A-Ju!

625
00:50:59,256 --> 00:51:01,458
Business is better for you today.

626
00:51:05,996 --> 00:51:06,864
A-Ju!

627
00:51:08,999 --> 00:51:12,202
Shall we go out together on Sunday?

628
00:51:13,270 --> 00:51:16,140
To the children’s amusement park?

629
00:51:16,407 --> 00:51:17,675
That’s right...

630
00:51:19,276 --> 00:51:20,411
I promise you.

631
00:51:20,611 --> 00:51:21,745
Really?

632
00:51:23,881 --> 00:51:24,949
A-Ju...

633
00:51:27,284 --> 00:51:28,686
You’re so pretty.

634
00:53:11,989 --> 00:53:13,390
The boys are really out of line.

635
00:53:13,724 --> 00:53:15,659
Not one of them is home on a Sunday.

636
00:53:17,327 --> 00:53:20,397
Dad, Second Brother went
to the children's amusement park.

637
00:53:20,664 --> 00:53:21,265
How do you know?

638
00:53:21,598 --> 00:53:24,268
He learned a few Taiwanese phrases
from me a few days ago.

639
00:53:24,601 --> 00:53:28,806
“Children’s amusement park.
Shall we go out and play on Sunday?”

640
00:53:29,073 --> 00:53:29,873
And...

641
00:53:30,140 --> 00:53:30,941
And what?

642
00:53:31,208 --> 00:53:33,143
Never mind, never mind. I won’t say.

643
00:53:43,487 --> 00:53:46,090
I wonder where Wuxiong and Meizhi went.

644
00:53:46,356 --> 00:53:48,492
Even A-Ju is out.

645
00:53:48,826 --> 00:53:51,361
When they get back,
I’ll give them a good scolding.

646
00:53:51,695 --> 00:53:55,632
Dad, A-Ju has been learning Mandarin
from me these past few days.

647
00:53:55,899 --> 00:53:57,234
Learning Mandarin from you?

648
00:53:57,501 --> 00:53:58,902
What did she learn?

649
00:53:59,169 --> 00:54:04,775
She keeps saying,
“I promise you, I promise you.”

650
00:54:05,109 --> 00:54:06,910
I wonder who she’s promising.

651
00:54:51,955 --> 00:54:54,158
Zenghong, shall we sit here for a while?

652
00:54:54,358 --> 00:54:55,225
All right.

653
00:55:15,112 --> 00:55:16,513
My cousin’s here.

654
00:55:16,780 --> 00:55:18,448
Why is she with my older brother?

655
00:55:18,715 --> 00:55:20,050
Your older brother?

656
00:55:20,317 --> 00:55:21,585
What a coincidence.

657
00:55:32,529 --> 00:55:34,331
That voice sounds familiar.

658
00:55:35,332 --> 00:55:37,734
It sounds like my cousin.

659
00:55:40,137 --> 00:55:43,207
Yes, it sounds just like Zenghong’s laugh.

660
00:55:43,473 --> 00:55:45,275
What would he be doing here?

661
00:55:47,211 --> 00:55:48,212
Let’s go have a look.

662
00:55:48,545 --> 00:55:50,814
Forget it. Never mind.

663
00:55:54,751 --> 00:55:56,019
A-Ju!

664
00:56:29,253 --> 00:56:30,254
A-Ju!

665
00:56:31,054 --> 00:56:34,324
I'm considering inviting my mother
over to your house.

666
00:56:34,591 --> 00:56:35,859
What for?

667
00:56:54,011 --> 00:56:56,146
So your brother is dating my cousin.

668
00:57:00,751 --> 00:57:03,353
A-Ju, go home and tell your mother

669
00:57:03,687 --> 00:57:05,756
that your big brother has a girlfriend.

670
00:57:06,156 --> 00:57:08,225
Then she can’t object to us, right?

671
00:57:08,492 --> 00:57:09,359
All right.

672
00:57:09,760 --> 00:57:10,894
Let’s go.

673
00:57:12,763 --> 00:57:14,898
Meizhi, I've been trying
to find your address.

674
00:57:15,165 --> 00:57:17,167
It turns out you live
right next door to us.

675
00:57:19,369 --> 00:57:21,104
My cousin and the others are coming again.

676
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:23,173
Quick, let’s hide over there.

677
00:57:23,507 --> 00:57:23,774
No...

678
00:57:54,871 --> 00:57:58,408
Wuxiong,
that man’s back looks just like my cousin.

679
00:58:00,744 --> 00:58:02,145
It’s Zenghong.

680
00:58:03,347 --> 00:58:05,749
That woman looks like my younger sister.

681
00:58:06,083 --> 00:58:07,617
Come on, let’s go take a look.

682
00:58:07,884 --> 00:58:08,752
All right.

683
00:58:18,161 --> 00:58:21,098
Cousin, you two look awfully affectionate!

684
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:25,102
Zenghong, you...

685
00:58:25,369 --> 00:58:28,038
You and my cousin got close awfully fast.

686
00:58:28,305 --> 00:58:29,840
You and my brother are no different.

687
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:32,642
What? He’s your brother?

688
00:58:33,910 --> 00:58:36,513
Zenghong, I hadn’t even introduced
my younger sister to you,

689
00:58:36,780 --> 00:58:38,048
and you’ve already met her.

690
00:58:38,315 --> 00:58:39,716
You’re quite a one!

691
00:58:50,727 --> 00:58:52,462
Why is my big brother here too?

692
00:58:52,729 --> 00:58:54,197
Isn’t that my older sister?

693
00:58:54,531 --> 00:58:55,732
Shall we go over and see her?

694
00:58:55,932 --> 00:58:56,666
All right.

695
00:58:56,933 --> 00:58:58,735
- Big Brother!
- Sis!

696
00:58:59,002 --> 00:58:59,870
Bro! Sis! A-Ju! Sis!

697
00:59:00,270 --> 00:59:01,738
Second Brother, you’re here too!

698
00:59:02,072 --> 00:59:03,473
Shall we all go play together?

699
00:59:03,740 --> 00:59:04,408
I’m all for it!

700
00:59:04,875 --> 00:59:06,076
All right...

701
01:02:29,613 --> 01:02:30,547
Huang!

702
01:02:31,348 --> 01:02:32,749
Huang!

703
01:02:33,283 --> 01:02:35,151
They’re back.

704
01:02:35,418 --> 01:02:37,020
Good. That’s good.

705
01:02:37,287 --> 01:02:38,421
Get up.

706
01:02:44,427 --> 01:02:46,096
This is bad.

707
01:02:46,496 --> 01:02:50,166
Our children now visit the neighbors—
who knows when that began.

708
01:02:50,567 --> 01:02:55,171
A daughter can’t be kept at home forever.
If things go too far, we’ll be in trouble.

709
01:02:57,841 --> 01:02:58,842
Is that really true?

710
01:02:59,109 --> 01:03:00,176
Yes.

711
01:03:00,777 --> 01:03:02,045
Let’s go see.

712
01:03:28,204 --> 01:03:30,740
Dad, you’re still up?

713
01:03:32,008 --> 01:03:33,276
Where did you take your sister?

714
01:03:33,543 --> 01:03:35,145
You’ve been out all day.
No one could find you.

715
01:03:35,412 --> 01:03:36,413
I...

716
01:03:36,680 --> 01:03:38,815
You two go to bed first.

717
01:03:39,082 --> 01:03:40,950
I have something to discuss
with your eldest brother.

718
01:03:54,431 --> 01:03:57,767
Wuxiong, you’re the eldest.

719
01:03:58,101 --> 01:04:02,572
You’ve graduated from college
and completed your military service.

720
01:04:03,573 --> 01:04:06,576
What are your plans for the future?

721
01:04:06,910 --> 01:04:08,978
Dad,
I have a classmate who lives next door.

722
01:04:09,312 --> 01:04:10,780
He’ll get me a construction job.

723
01:04:11,047 --> 01:04:13,183
The neighbors?

724
01:04:13,450 --> 01:04:14,517
That’s what I wanted to ask.

725
01:04:14,851 --> 01:04:15,985
Just because he got you a job,

726
01:04:16,319 --> 01:04:20,657
does that mean you can take
your sister out with him?

727
01:04:21,991 --> 01:04:25,395
Yes. He’s an upright man,
and he studied medicine.

728
01:04:25,729 --> 01:04:27,597
Why can't we spend time with him?

729
01:04:27,931 --> 01:04:31,468
Does that count as real medical training?

730
01:04:31,801 --> 01:04:34,137
My daughter won't associate with them.

731
01:04:34,404 --> 01:04:35,939
Dad, he’s not a Chinese medicine doctor.

732
01:04:36,272 --> 01:04:38,007
He’s a Western doctor, an NTU graduate.

733
01:04:38,274 --> 01:04:41,010
A Western doctor? Well, that’s different.

734
01:04:41,277 --> 01:04:42,879
What do you mean, “that’s different”?

735
01:04:43,146 --> 01:04:44,614
He’s a Mainlander.

736
01:04:44,948 --> 01:04:47,150
If our daughter marries away,
I’ll never get to see her again.

737
01:04:47,484 --> 01:04:51,354
Mom, don’t worry.
Transportation is so convenient nowadays.

738
01:04:51,755 --> 01:04:57,293
In the future, we can fly to Shanghai
or Nanjing in just a few dozen minutes.

739
01:04:57,627 --> 01:05:00,296
It’ll be no farther
than going to Kaohsiung.

740
01:05:00,630 --> 01:05:03,767
Mom, don’t you always say
you want to visit Shanghai?

741
01:05:04,100 --> 01:05:06,236
If we have relatives living in Shanghai,

742
01:05:06,503 --> 01:05:08,238
wouldn’t that make things more convenient?

743
01:05:10,573 --> 01:05:13,376
Well, that does make some sense.

744
01:05:13,710 --> 01:05:16,780
Perhaps we should let them see
each other as friends first.

745
01:05:17,113 --> 01:05:19,783
The eldest daughter next door
is my cousin’s classmate.

746
01:05:20,116 --> 01:05:22,452
Big Brother and the eldest son
next door are classmates too.

747
01:05:22,786 --> 01:05:24,921
Big Brother likes their eldest daughter.

748
01:05:25,255 --> 01:05:28,258
The eldest son next door likes our cousin.

749
01:05:28,525 --> 01:05:30,860
I like A-Ju next door.

750
01:05:31,194 --> 01:05:33,263
And A-Ju next door likes me too.

751
01:05:35,398 --> 01:05:37,667
All right... That’s enough...

752
01:05:38,001 --> 01:05:42,138
This whole tangled mess is getting
more confusing the more I hear.

753
01:05:43,940 --> 01:05:45,208
I’m warning you all.

754
01:05:45,475 --> 01:05:47,076
Don’t go fooling around outside.

755
01:05:47,410 --> 01:05:49,212
We haven’t even lived here that long.

756
01:05:49,479 --> 01:05:51,481
We can’t let the neighbors laugh at us.

757
01:05:51,748 --> 01:05:53,082
It’s late.

758
01:05:53,349 --> 01:05:55,018
I’m going to bed.

759
01:05:55,285 --> 01:05:56,886
Talk to your mother if you need anything.

760
01:05:57,220 --> 01:06:01,491
Lately, A-Ju has been spending time
with the neighbors.

761
01:06:01,758 --> 01:06:03,827
If he marries her,
what will become of you?

762
01:06:04,160 --> 01:06:06,429
Mom, A-Ju is my younger sister.

763
01:06:06,763 --> 01:06:09,899
Since she has someone she loves,
we should help her be with him.

764
01:06:10,166 --> 01:06:12,769
Mom, why don’t you go and ask them?

765
01:06:13,770 --> 01:06:15,505
I don’t think they’ll agree.

766
01:06:15,772 --> 01:06:17,240
Why let a good thing go to an outsider?

767
01:06:17,574 --> 01:06:19,108
They’ll let you marry A-Ju.

768
01:06:19,375 --> 01:06:20,510
Just go and ask.

769
01:06:20,844 --> 01:06:23,847
You’re getting more shameless by the day.

770
01:06:24,113 --> 01:06:25,982
You’re so impatient.

771
01:06:26,249 --> 01:06:28,318
Mrs. Huang is very stubborn.

772
01:06:28,585 --> 01:06:29,853
You want me to go and get rejected?

773
01:06:30,119 --> 01:06:32,789
Forget it. Absolutely not.

774
01:06:33,122 --> 01:06:36,125
I raised A-Ju through so much hardship.

775
01:06:36,392 --> 01:06:37,794
You expect me to give her away for free?

776
01:06:38,061 --> 01:06:38,995
Absolutely not!

777
01:06:39,329 --> 01:06:41,264
Mom, marriage is a matter of choice now.

778
01:06:41,531 --> 01:06:42,866
How can you force her?

779
01:06:44,334 --> 01:06:46,536
How can you be so unreasonable?

780
01:06:46,870 --> 01:06:50,139
A-Ju is indispensable to this family.

781
01:06:50,473 --> 01:06:53,676
If she gets married, who'll handle
the nursing, cooking, and laundry?

782
01:06:53,943 --> 01:06:54,811
Who’ll do it all?

783
01:06:55,144 --> 01:06:58,014
Where could you find a daughter-in-law
as good as her?

784
01:07:00,350 --> 01:07:04,821
I’ll make the decision.
You two will get married next month.

785
01:07:05,088 --> 01:07:06,289
All right. Go to bed.

786
01:07:06,623 --> 01:07:08,558
Just go next door
and say a few kind words.

787
01:07:08,825 --> 01:07:09,559
Go on!

788
01:07:11,094 --> 01:07:12,562
You’ve lost your mind.

789
01:07:12,896 --> 01:07:14,898
Where do you expect
me to go at this hour of the night?

790
01:07:15,164 --> 01:07:16,766
We can’t go until tomorrow,
at the earliest.

791
01:07:17,033 --> 01:07:18,968
Fine. Tomorrow, then.

792
01:07:19,636 --> 01:07:21,571
Honestly, you...

793
01:07:35,785 --> 01:07:37,520
Dr. Huang, thank you so much.

794
01:07:37,854 --> 01:07:39,188
Ever since that last injection,

795
01:07:39,522 --> 01:07:41,991
My aches and pains have improved a lot.

796
01:07:42,325 --> 01:07:45,528
Since it’s helping,
you can come every day.

797
01:07:45,795 --> 01:07:47,063
I’m sorry to trouble you.

798
01:07:47,330 --> 01:07:48,264
Don’t mention it.

799
01:07:50,199 --> 01:07:53,403
Dr. Huang, there’s something else
I’d like to discuss with you.

800
01:07:53,670 --> 01:07:55,738
Whatever it is, please go ahead.

801
01:08:07,684 --> 01:08:10,687
This is a decision that will affect
our children for the rest of their lives.

802
01:08:10,954 --> 01:08:12,555
I’ll have to think it over.

803
01:08:14,223 --> 01:08:16,626
Our children are already in love.

804
01:08:16,960 --> 01:08:19,429
Why shouldn’t we parents
help them be together?

805
01:08:19,696 --> 01:08:20,897
You’re very open-minded.

806
01:08:21,164 --> 01:08:23,166
That’s why you became a Western doctor,
after all.

807
01:08:24,968 --> 01:08:30,506
All right. In principle, I’m not opposed.

808
01:08:31,240 --> 01:08:32,442
We’ll discuss it again later.

809
01:08:32,709 --> 01:08:35,244
We’ll talk about it again another time.

810
01:08:46,322 --> 01:08:47,123
Auntie!

811
01:08:47,457 --> 01:08:49,125
What are you doing here?

812
01:08:49,392 --> 01:08:50,660
Me?

813
01:08:52,195 --> 01:08:53,997
Nothing, nothing.

814
01:08:56,799 --> 01:08:57,867
I’ll be going.

815
01:09:01,004 --> 01:09:02,405
Where’s your father?

816
01:09:03,206 --> 01:09:04,540
He’s inside.

817
01:09:10,480 --> 01:09:12,615
I’m sorry to keep troubling you.

818
01:09:12,815 --> 01:09:13,883
It’s no trouble.

819
01:09:14,150 --> 01:09:16,953
Just come by at this time every day,

820
01:09:17,220 --> 01:09:18,755
and I’ll give you an injection.

821
01:09:19,022 --> 01:09:21,090
All right. You’re very kind.

822
01:09:21,357 --> 01:09:23,159
Your wife, though, is harder to deal with.

823
01:09:23,493 --> 01:09:26,629
The last time I came,
she looked very angry.

824
01:09:26,896 --> 01:09:28,164
Just ignore her.

825
01:09:30,633 --> 01:09:33,503
You’ve got some nerve,
talking about me behind my back!

826
01:09:36,105 --> 01:09:38,508
Mrs. Huang, you’ve misunderstood!

827
01:09:38,775 --> 01:09:39,909
What have I misunderstood?

828
01:09:41,310 --> 01:09:42,912
I heard it with my own ears!

829
01:09:44,113 --> 01:09:45,782
You think you can get away with anything.

830
01:09:48,251 --> 01:09:50,386
- Get away with anything?
- It’s a misunderstanding!

831
01:09:50,653 --> 01:09:51,854
How can you be so uncivilized?

832
01:09:52,121 --> 01:09:53,790
Mrs. Chen, I’m terribly sorry.

833
01:09:54,524 --> 01:09:55,525
Why did you hit me?

834
01:09:55,792 --> 01:09:57,927
- It was a misunderstanding!
- What misunderstanding?

835
01:09:58,261 --> 01:09:58,861
- Mrs. Chen!
- Why hit me?

836
01:09:59,195 --> 01:10:01,330
I’m sorry, I’m sorry.
It was a misunderstanding.

837
01:10:06,469 --> 01:10:07,870
You crazy woman! You lunatic!

838
01:10:08,137 --> 01:10:09,539
Why did you hit me?

839
01:10:09,806 --> 01:10:11,074
Good grief! What is wrong with you?

840
01:10:11,407 --> 01:10:13,209
No need to apologize! No more shots!
It’s a misunderstanding!

841
01:10:13,409 --> 01:10:14,744
It’s a misunderstanding!

842
01:10:15,011 --> 01:10:16,412
Honestly, you...

843
01:10:18,881 --> 01:10:20,349
What’s going on outside?

844
01:10:21,951 --> 01:10:23,019
She’s still yelling!

845
01:10:24,487 --> 01:10:26,155
You crazy woman! You lunatic!

846
01:10:36,699 --> 01:10:38,101
You crazy woman!

847
01:10:42,105 --> 01:10:43,372
My husband isn’t home.

848
01:10:46,442 --> 01:10:48,444
You’re taking advantage of the fact
that he’s away!

849
01:10:51,047 --> 01:10:51,714
- Let go!
- I’ll hit you!

850
01:10:52,048 --> 01:10:53,516
- You little hoodlum!
- I’ll hit you!

851
01:10:53,783 --> 01:10:54,984
You little delinquent!

852
01:10:55,251 --> 01:10:56,519
Xiaolong... Xiaoli...

853
01:10:56,853 --> 01:10:57,787
Mom!

854
01:11:00,656 --> 01:11:02,658
You Huang woman, don’t push me around!

855
01:11:02,925 --> 01:11:04,060
Who’s pushing whom around?

856
01:11:04,393 --> 01:11:06,262
Shameless! You’ve got no shame!

857
01:11:06,596 --> 01:11:08,064
You’re the shameless one!

858
01:11:08,397 --> 01:11:10,266
A shameless person is shameless!

859
01:11:10,600 --> 01:11:12,668
What? You want to fight, is that it?

860
01:11:12,935 --> 01:11:14,470
I’m not afraid of you!

861
01:11:14,737 --> 01:11:16,939
You act as if your husband
were some kind of quack!

862
01:11:17,206 --> 01:11:18,341
A quack?

863
01:11:18,608 --> 01:11:19,809
What kind of man is your husband?

864
01:11:20,143 --> 01:11:23,146
He knows a few words of Japanese
and pretends he studied in Japan.

865
01:11:23,479 --> 01:11:25,348
He’s nothing but a fake doctor,
an unlicensed quack!

866
01:11:26,482 --> 01:11:29,886
Don’t make false accusations!
Keep it up and I’ll sue you!

867
01:11:30,153 --> 01:11:31,420
Sue me? For what?

868
01:11:31,687 --> 01:11:33,422
For seducing my husband!

869
01:11:33,689 --> 01:11:34,557
What did you say?

870
01:11:34,891 --> 01:11:36,492
What did I say? I’m done talking to you.

871
01:11:36,759 --> 01:11:38,227
I’ll have my husband deal with you.

872
01:11:38,494 --> 01:11:39,295
Come on!

873
01:11:44,634 --> 01:11:45,835
Come along, Xiaoli.

874
01:11:49,372 --> 01:11:52,375
The neighbors say you’re a fake doctor.

875
01:11:52,642 --> 01:11:56,312
A fake? Who cares?

876
01:11:57,847 --> 01:12:00,116
Even you’re taking her side?

877
01:12:00,449 --> 01:12:02,919
Have you forgotten
that our children are grown up now?

878
01:12:03,252 --> 01:12:06,255
You’re already halfway into your grave,
and you’re still carrying on like this!

879
01:12:07,123 --> 01:12:08,524
Why are you so suspicious?

880
01:12:08,791 --> 01:12:11,594
Mrs. Chen came here to get an injection.

881
01:12:11,861 --> 01:12:13,596
An injection? What kind of injection?

882
01:12:13,863 --> 01:12:16,399
She said her back was aching.

883
01:12:16,732 --> 01:12:19,468
I can’t believe
she insulted you like that,

884
01:12:19,735 --> 01:12:20,670
And you did nothing!

885
01:12:21,003 --> 01:12:22,939
Come with me. Let's settle this with her!

886
01:12:23,206 --> 01:12:24,207
Forget it. Don’t make a scene.

887
01:12:24,473 --> 01:12:27,276
Neighbors should live together in harmony.

888
01:12:27,677 --> 01:12:30,746
No! Why should I tolerate such an insult?

889
01:12:31,080 --> 01:12:33,349
Go over and ask her what she meant!

890
01:12:33,616 --> 01:12:35,418
Forget it, forget it.

891
01:12:35,751 --> 01:12:38,888
Forget it?
She's still calling you a quack!

892
01:12:39,155 --> 01:12:40,156
A red-turbaned Indian cop?

893
01:12:40,423 --> 01:12:41,891
What do you mean,
a red-turbaned Indian cop?

894
01:12:42,158 --> 01:12:44,493
A-Zhu told me that means a quack doctor.

895
01:12:44,760 --> 01:12:46,162
A quack doctor?

896
01:12:47,230 --> 01:12:49,098
She called me a duck?

897
01:12:49,365 --> 01:12:50,967
Then what is he, anyway?

898
01:12:51,234 --> 01:12:53,236
Come on. Let’s go find her.

899
01:13:01,444 --> 01:13:02,912
Go settle it yourself, then.

900
01:13:03,846 --> 01:13:05,381
Come on, let’s go together.

901
01:13:10,720 --> 01:13:12,922
Mr. Chen, how are you?

902
01:13:13,990 --> 01:13:15,725
Mr. Huang, how are you?

903
01:13:16,592 --> 01:13:17,994
I came to see you.

904
01:13:18,261 --> 01:13:23,199
Step on me?
You want to step on me with your foot?

905
01:13:23,466 --> 01:13:27,003
No, I came to see you.

906
01:13:27,203 --> 01:13:27,737
You came for me?

907
01:13:28,070 --> 01:13:30,673
That’s right.
I was just about to step on you, too.

908
01:13:31,007 --> 01:13:32,141
- Come to my place.
- No, mine.

909
01:13:32,408 --> 01:13:33,943
Come to our house.

910
01:13:34,277 --> 01:13:36,078
Why go to their house? Come to ours!

911
01:13:36,946 --> 01:13:38,347
Come over here!

912
01:13:39,081 --> 01:13:41,417
Why should we go to their house?
We should go to ours!

913
01:14:08,778 --> 01:14:09,979
Let’s sit down and talk.

914
01:14:10,246 --> 01:14:11,380
Let’s talk inside our house.

915
01:14:12,114 --> 01:14:13,182
It’s the same if we talk here.

916
01:14:13,449 --> 01:14:14,717
I’m going home.

917
01:14:14,917 --> 01:14:16,385
Women are always like this.

918
01:14:21,724 --> 01:14:22,658
Go on, say it!

919
01:14:23,259 --> 01:14:24,994
You explain it to him.

920
01:14:25,261 --> 01:14:28,864
She says she insulted her,
and she insulted me too.

921
01:14:29,198 --> 01:14:31,734
She says she insulted her,
and she insulted me too!

922
01:14:32,068 --> 01:14:34,203
What? When did I insult him?

923
01:14:34,537 --> 01:14:35,404
What did I say about you?

924
01:14:35,671 --> 01:14:37,073
What did I say about him? Tell me!

925
01:14:37,340 --> 01:14:39,141
You crazy woman!

926
01:14:39,475 --> 01:14:41,610
What do you mean, crazy woman?
You’re the crazy one!

927
01:14:41,877 --> 01:14:43,012
- Crazy woman!
- You too!

928
01:14:43,279 --> 01:14:43,879
Misunderstanding!

929
01:14:44,146 --> 01:14:46,882
- See? She’s still insulting me!
- Quiet!

930
01:14:47,883 --> 01:14:49,618
Xiaoli, get out of the way.

931
01:14:51,887 --> 01:14:54,690
No! I won’t leave until
she apologizes to me today!

932
01:14:55,024 --> 01:14:57,026
Why did she hit me for no reason?

933
01:14:57,293 --> 01:14:59,161
Then accuse me of seducing her husband!

934
01:14:59,428 --> 01:15:01,097
You think your husband is some pretty boy?

935
01:15:01,364 --> 01:15:02,431
What would I want with him?

936
01:15:02,765 --> 01:15:04,100
He’s the only thing I like about him!

937
01:15:05,034 --> 01:15:06,702
You crazy woman! You shrew!

938
01:15:06,969 --> 01:15:08,771
What do you mean, “shrew”?

939
01:15:09,105 --> 01:15:10,840
Your husband is a skinny monkey!

940
01:15:11,173 --> 01:15:12,708
- A loquat?
- What loquat? A lychee!

941
01:15:12,975 --> 01:15:13,776
Don’t argue with her.

942
01:15:14,110 --> 01:15:15,111
Tell him to look in a mirror!

943
01:15:15,444 --> 01:15:16,779
Call me a shrew again, you shrew!

944
01:15:17,113 --> 01:15:18,714
- What do you mean, shrew?
- That’s enough!

945
01:15:24,387 --> 01:15:25,454
Blood!

946
01:15:28,724 --> 01:15:30,126
- Xiaolong!
- What is it?

947
01:15:30,459 --> 01:15:31,927
Your parents and my parents

948
01:15:32,194 --> 01:15:34,530
are fighting at our house.
They’re all bleeding!

949
01:15:34,797 --> 01:15:35,798
Really?

950
01:15:36,065 --> 01:15:36,866
Really!

951
01:15:39,735 --> 01:15:40,936
Sis!

952
01:15:41,203 --> 01:15:42,471
Xiaolong, what is it?

953
01:15:42,805 --> 01:15:45,541
Mom and Dad are fighting next door.
They’re bleeding!

954
01:15:45,875 --> 01:15:47,343
- Is that true?
- Yes!

955
01:15:51,147 --> 01:15:55,084
Your parents and mine are fighting
at your house,

956
01:15:55,418 --> 01:15:57,620
- and they’re bleeding!
- What?

957
01:15:57,887 --> 01:15:59,288
- They’re bleeding?
- Yes!

958
01:16:09,498 --> 01:16:11,033
Then we’ll have to split
up and find everyone.

959
01:16:11,300 --> 01:16:12,568
Call your older sister right away.

960
01:16:12,902 --> 01:16:14,170
- You go get Big Brother.
- All right.

961
01:16:14,437 --> 01:16:15,905
- You go find Miss Liang.
- Okay.

962
01:16:16,172 --> 01:16:17,173
You go get your brother.

963
01:16:17,440 --> 01:16:18,307
Hurry!

964
01:16:57,746 --> 01:17:01,350
Let’s call today’s gathering a joint
meeting of our two families.

965
01:17:02,284 --> 01:17:05,087
We were good friends and good
neighbors to begin with.

966
01:17:05,421 --> 01:17:08,290
I practice Chinese medicine,
and Mr. Huang practices Western medicine.

967
01:17:08,624 --> 01:17:10,226
Our methods may be different,

968
01:17:10,493 --> 01:17:11,827
but our goal is the same.

969
01:17:12,094 --> 01:17:13,496
Isn’t that right, Mr. Huang?

970
01:17:13,696 --> 01:17:14,763
That’s right.

971
01:17:15,431 --> 01:17:19,034
Chinese medicine has its strengths,

972
01:17:19,301 --> 01:17:21,504
and Western medicine has its shortcomings.

973
01:17:21,770 --> 01:17:23,506
Its strong points...

974
01:17:23,839 --> 01:17:26,775
We’re all here to save lives
and help people, aren’t we?

975
01:17:27,109 --> 01:17:31,380
But someone has been calling me names
behind my back... What did they call me?

976
01:17:31,714 --> 01:17:35,784
A quack. A-Zhu told me
that's what they call a fake doctor.

977
01:17:36,051 --> 01:17:37,386
That made me very angry.

978
01:17:37,720 --> 01:17:42,324
Some people say nice things to my face,

979
01:17:42,658 --> 01:17:46,929
but behind my back,
they call me an unlicensed doctor.

980
01:17:47,196 --> 01:17:50,599
I understand.
“Unlicensed doctor” means a fake doctor.

981
01:17:50,866 --> 01:17:52,668
It’s really ridiculous.

982
01:17:52,868 --> 01:17:54,336
Ridiculous!

983
01:17:55,204 --> 01:17:57,540
My father was a famous
physician in Jiangnan.

984
01:17:57,873 --> 01:17:59,675
My grandfather was a Qing
imperial physician.

985
01:18:00,009 --> 01:18:02,478
He even treated Emperor Guangxu!

986
01:18:02,745 --> 01:18:04,747
I have our family tree to prove it.

987
01:18:05,014 --> 01:18:06,282
No need, no need.

988
01:18:06,615 --> 01:18:10,553
I have a medical
doctorate from the University of Tokyo.

989
01:18:10,886 --> 01:18:14,089
I have my diploma
and photographs to prove it.

990
01:18:14,356 --> 01:18:16,425
I’m no fake, either.

991
01:18:17,159 --> 01:18:19,695
Yes... I believe this is another
misunderstanding.

992
01:18:19,962 --> 01:18:21,697
Yes... a misunderstanding.

993
01:18:40,849 --> 01:18:43,652
Brother! Brother! Brother!

994
01:18:44,320 --> 01:18:46,121
Xiaolong, what are you doing here?

995
01:18:46,388 --> 01:18:47,656
Bad news! Hurry home!

996
01:18:47,923 --> 01:18:48,524
What happened?

997
01:18:48,724 --> 01:18:50,726
Mom and Dad are fighting our neighbors!

998
01:18:50,993 --> 01:18:52,127
They’re beating each other bloody!

999
01:18:52,394 --> 01:18:52,795
Really?

1000
01:18:53,062 --> 01:18:53,996
Really!

1001
01:18:58,133 --> 01:19:01,804
Mr. Huang is one of Taiwan's top GPs.

1002
01:19:02,137 --> 01:19:06,408
Your surgical work is especially renowned.

1003
01:19:06,675 --> 01:19:08,077
You flatter me.

1004
01:19:08,410 --> 01:19:12,414
Brother Xiting, you're a renowned
Chinese medicine doctor too.

1005
01:19:12,681 --> 01:19:14,283
Everyone knows that.

1006
01:19:14,550 --> 01:19:16,018
Not at all, not at all.

1007
01:19:16,352 --> 01:19:19,421
Western medicine is certainly effective

1008
01:19:19,688 --> 01:19:21,090
for surgery and acute illnesses.

1009
01:19:21,490 --> 01:19:24,827
But for internal conditions
involving several ailments at once,

1010
01:19:25,094 --> 01:19:26,562
it can’t match Chinese medicine.

1011
01:19:26,895 --> 01:19:31,834
That’s not true. Chinese medicine
is fine for minor complaints,

1012
01:19:32,167 --> 01:19:36,105
but serious illnesses still
require Western medicine.

1013
01:19:36,438 --> 01:19:40,643
Chinese medicine is outdated nowadays.

1014
01:19:40,909 --> 01:19:42,645
That’s completely wrong!

1015
01:19:42,978 --> 01:19:44,980
Chinese medicine has its own mysteries.

1016
01:19:48,717 --> 01:19:51,520
You have to start learning
Chinese medicine as a child.

1017
01:19:51,854 --> 01:19:54,189
It takes decades of experience before
you can call yourself a doctor.

1018
01:19:54,523 --> 01:19:58,260
Unlike Western doctors, who think
a few wonder drugs make them doctors.

1019
01:19:58,594 --> 01:20:02,398
And there are so many fake medicines now.
Take the wrong one and you're done for!

1020
01:20:04,667 --> 01:20:09,605
What a joke! What do you know?
I’m done talking to you.

1021
01:20:09,938 --> 01:20:14,276
We Western doctors can perform surgery.
Can you?

1022
01:20:14,610 --> 01:20:17,146
Surgery? That’s easy!

1023
01:20:17,413 --> 01:20:18,614
Just sterilize everything properly,

1024
01:20:18,947 --> 01:20:21,150
then cut out the rotten parts.

1025
01:20:21,483 --> 01:20:24,086
Buy a few corpses
and practice dissecting them,

1026
01:20:24,353 --> 01:20:25,421
and you’ll learn in no time.

1027
01:20:25,688 --> 01:20:26,889
Chinese medicine has its secrets.

1028
01:20:27,289 --> 01:20:31,760
It can make the damaged parts of your body
heal themselves little by little.

1029
01:20:32,027 --> 01:20:35,631
That’s quite an exaggeration.
What nonsense!

1030
01:20:35,898 --> 01:20:37,966
Nonsense? How can you call that nonsense?

1031
01:20:38,367 --> 01:20:41,970
You’re just suffering from a complex
that makes you worship everything foreign.

1032
01:20:44,973 --> 01:20:48,243
Western medicine
was developed by foreigners.

1033
01:20:48,577 --> 01:20:51,513
You think the moon abroad is always
rounder than the moon at home,

1034
01:20:51,847 --> 01:20:54,316
and that another man’s wife
is better than your own.

1035
01:20:55,517 --> 01:20:59,922
Another man’s wife is better
than your own wife...

1036
01:21:00,255 --> 01:21:01,790
What is that supposed to mean?

1037
01:21:02,124 --> 01:21:03,792
Are you insulting me?

1038
01:21:04,126 --> 01:21:06,862
You're insulting me in front of my wife!

1039
01:21:07,196 --> 01:21:10,799
I was giving your wife an injection.
That’s all.

1040
01:21:11,066 --> 01:21:12,868
Who knows what you were thinking?

1041
01:21:13,202 --> 01:21:15,871
All right, we haven’t discussed
anything serious at all.

1042
01:21:16,138 --> 01:21:16,939
Why bother?

1043
01:21:17,206 --> 01:21:18,207
Sit down.

1044
01:21:20,342 --> 01:21:22,611
Big Brother! Big Brother!
Hurry home! What happened?

1045
01:21:23,011 --> 01:21:25,881
Dad and Mom are fighting our neighbors!

1046
01:21:26,148 --> 01:21:27,883
- Really?
- Really!

1047
01:21:28,150 --> 01:21:29,218
Come on!

1048
01:21:38,761 --> 01:21:43,365
All right, Brother Ximing.
Our differences are merely

1049
01:21:43,632 --> 01:21:45,768
academic disagreements.

1050
01:21:46,101 --> 01:21:48,504
It’s a perfectly reasonable debate.

1051
01:21:48,771 --> 01:21:49,972
Please don’t take offense.

1052
01:21:50,239 --> 01:21:53,509
Take offense? Not at all.

1053
01:21:53,842 --> 01:21:57,513
I’m quite happy to accept your criticism.

1054
01:22:05,921 --> 01:22:08,056
- Second Brother!
- A-Ju, what’s happened to Dad?

1055
01:22:08,390 --> 01:22:10,592
I don’t know. They’re both inside,
and it’s completely quiet.

1056
01:22:10,859 --> 01:22:12,528
I don’t know what’s going on.

1057
01:22:14,797 --> 01:22:19,268
Dad! Mom!

1058
01:22:23,005 --> 01:22:27,743
If anything happens to my parents,
I’ll hold you responsible!

1059
01:22:28,010 --> 01:22:29,144
What does that have to do with me?

1060
01:22:29,478 --> 01:22:32,481
This is all your fault!
Don’t be like that.

1061
01:22:33,348 --> 01:22:35,150
Can you stop being so unreasonable?

1062
01:22:35,484 --> 01:22:36,752
Unreasonable? Don’t...

1063
01:22:37,085 --> 01:22:38,287
Why did you push me?

1064
01:22:39,822 --> 01:22:41,290
Can’t you be reasonable?

1065
01:22:41,557 --> 01:22:42,624
What do you mean, reasonable?

1066
01:22:45,694 --> 01:22:48,030
Why did you push me?
Are you looking for a fight?

1067
01:22:56,104 --> 01:22:57,239
Come on, then!

1068
01:22:57,506 --> 01:22:58,307
Brother!

1069
01:22:58,907 --> 01:23:00,108
Don’t!

1070
01:23:02,778 --> 01:23:03,912
You’d better not come any closer!

1071
01:23:05,714 --> 01:23:07,182
Don’t! This is bad!

1072
01:23:07,449 --> 01:23:09,985
Don’t! Stop it! This is terrible!

1073
01:23:10,252 --> 01:23:11,186
Brother!

1074
01:23:12,321 --> 01:23:14,323
Mrs. Huang, you speak first.

1075
01:23:14,590 --> 01:23:15,858
No, Mrs. Chen should speak first.

1076
01:23:16,124 --> 01:23:18,994
- You go first.
- No, you go first.

1077
01:23:19,261 --> 01:23:20,929
- Please, you go first.
- No, you go ahead.

1078
01:23:21,597 --> 01:23:23,465
You should speak first.

1079
01:23:29,071 --> 01:23:30,339
I...

1080
01:23:32,741 --> 01:23:34,743
It was all my fault.

1081
01:23:36,945 --> 01:23:39,681
We simply couldn’t understand
what one another was saying.

1082
01:23:42,351 --> 01:23:43,952
Now it’s your turn to stand up and speak.

1083
01:23:46,488 --> 01:23:51,159
This was entirely my fault.
Please accept my apology.

1084
01:23:51,760 --> 01:23:53,228
There’s no need for that.

1085
01:24:05,307 --> 01:24:07,843
A fight can turn strangers into friends.

1086
01:24:08,110 --> 01:24:09,711
Fate brings even enemies together.

1087
01:24:10,646 --> 01:24:13,715
I was at fault, too.

1088
01:24:14,049 --> 01:24:16,385
All right,
enough with the polite apologies.

1089
01:24:16,718 --> 01:24:19,121
Let’s talk about
our children’s future instead.

1090
01:24:20,055 --> 01:24:25,727
As for the marriage arrangements,
I’ll have to ask my wife.

1091
01:24:27,329 --> 01:24:32,067
But... you’re Mainlanders.

1092
01:24:32,334 --> 01:24:33,402
Mainlanders?

1093
01:24:34,202 --> 01:24:35,871
Mrs. Huang says we’re Mainlanders.

1094
01:24:36,204 --> 01:24:38,273
Aren't Mainlanders and Taiwanese alike?

1095
01:24:38,607 --> 01:24:40,475
We just have trouble understanding
one another’s speech.

1096
01:24:40,742 --> 01:24:42,477
We’re all Chinese, after all.

1097
01:24:45,013 --> 01:24:46,949
I know, I know.

1098
01:24:47,215 --> 01:24:48,884
Please, don’t say any more.

1099
01:24:50,285 --> 01:24:55,557
I’m very much in favor of marriages
between Taiwanese and Mainlanders.

1100
01:25:23,585 --> 01:25:26,188
I think that if we arrange
our children’s marriages

1101
01:25:26,521 --> 01:25:29,658
this way, it would be ideal.

1102
01:25:29,992 --> 01:25:33,862
Then we'd lose out: both your daughters
would marry into our family.

1103
01:25:34,262 --> 01:25:37,933
No... Isn’t our niece close to Wuxiong?

1104
01:25:38,266 --> 01:25:41,269
She was our eldest son's girlfriend first,

1105
01:25:41,603 --> 01:25:44,473
and now she's even found Wuxiong a job.

1106
01:25:44,806 --> 01:25:47,009
It really is a match made in heaven.

1107
01:25:50,212 --> 01:25:53,215
We don't ask for a bride price,

1108
01:25:53,482 --> 01:25:56,418
but we do require
a thousand boxes of wedding cakes.

1109
01:25:56,752 --> 01:25:58,887
What? A thousand boxes of what?

1110
01:25:59,154 --> 01:26:01,423
Wedding cakes.

1111
01:26:01,823 --> 01:26:06,294
Wedding cakes? Those big mooncakes
with lard inside?

1112
01:26:06,762 --> 01:26:07,229
Yes...

1113
01:26:07,496 --> 01:26:09,498
What’s so good about eating those?

1114
01:26:09,765 --> 01:26:13,235
A thousand boxes would cost
nearly twenty thousand dollars!

1115
01:26:13,502 --> 01:26:14,770
What’s the point of that?

1116
01:26:15,037 --> 01:26:16,972
It’s a Taiwanese custom.

1117
01:26:17,305 --> 01:26:20,776
What kind of custom?
It’s a terrible old practice!

1118
01:26:21,109 --> 01:26:25,113
A bad practice? No, it’s a fine custom!

1119
01:26:25,380 --> 01:26:27,249
No... It really is a bad practice!

1120
01:26:27,516 --> 01:26:28,917
It’s a custom!

1121
01:26:29,184 --> 01:26:29,651
A bad practice!

1122
01:26:29,918 --> 01:26:33,188
- It’s a custom!
- It’s a bad practice!

1123
01:26:33,922 --> 01:26:36,658
As long as the young people
truly love each other,

1124
01:26:36,925 --> 01:26:37,793
Then let them marry.

1125
01:26:38,193 --> 01:26:41,930
Why should we older people have to spend
so much money buying cakes for everyone?

1126
01:26:42,264 --> 01:26:45,200
There’s no way around it.
That’s how it has to be.

1127
01:26:46,068 --> 01:26:47,869
This character is really stubborn!

1128
01:26:48,136 --> 01:26:52,407
Character? Are you calling me a symbol?

1129
01:26:53,008 --> 01:26:54,609
Who’s calling you that?

1130
01:26:54,876 --> 01:26:57,679
You called me a symbol!

1131
01:26:58,080 --> 01:27:02,551
You Mainlanders use “character”
to mean a written symbol, not a person!

1132
01:27:02,818 --> 01:27:04,086
Then what are you, if not a symbol?

1133
01:27:04,419 --> 01:27:07,089
Well... I’m not a symbol.
That’s not what I meant.

1134
01:27:07,422 --> 01:27:11,293
“Character” isn’t an insult.
It’s just an expression.

1135
01:27:11,626 --> 01:27:13,962
Now you’re calling me a dog’s head?

1136
01:27:14,229 --> 01:27:15,564
You skinny monkey!

1137
01:27:15,897 --> 01:27:18,567
What? You called me a mountain dog!

1138
01:27:18,834 --> 01:27:19,768
You’re the dog!

1139
01:27:20,102 --> 01:27:21,570
- You skinny monkey!
- You mountain dog!

1140
01:27:21,837 --> 01:27:22,571
- Skinny monkey!
- Dog!

1141
01:27:22,838 --> 01:27:24,906
- Skinny monkey!
- Dog!

1142
01:27:25,173 --> 01:27:26,174
You’re ridiculous!

1143
01:27:26,441 --> 01:27:27,309
You’re the ridiculous one!

1144
01:27:27,576 --> 01:27:29,578
All right, that’s enough!

1145
01:27:29,911 --> 01:27:31,980
Don’t get angry. Let’s talk calmly.

1146
01:27:32,247 --> 01:27:35,183
That’s right. It was a misunderstanding.

1147
01:27:36,985 --> 01:27:38,320
Stop fighting!

1148
01:27:38,587 --> 01:27:40,989
Stop it! Don’t fight anymore, Brother!

1149
01:27:41,323 --> 01:27:42,791
You came just in time! He’s bullying me!

1150
01:27:44,192 --> 01:27:46,061
- Stop fighting!
- Why did you push me?

1151
01:27:46,328 --> 01:27:47,329
Why are you pushing me?

1152
01:27:48,864 --> 01:27:49,998
Why are you being so unreasonable?

1153
01:27:50,265 --> 01:27:51,800
You two brothers are ganging up on me!

1154
01:27:53,869 --> 01:27:55,003
Get off me!

1155
01:28:01,076 --> 01:28:02,878
You two are bullying my brother!

1156
01:28:03,478 --> 01:28:04,279
What’s going on here?

1157
01:28:05,747 --> 01:28:06,882
Stop fighting!

1158
01:28:08,483 --> 01:28:09,885
Stop it!

1159
01:28:10,152 --> 01:28:11,486
Don’t fight anymore!

1160
01:28:11,753 --> 01:28:16,358
Zenghong... Wake up!

1161
01:28:16,691 --> 01:28:18,827
I’m sorry. I didn’t mean to.

1162
01:28:37,579 --> 01:28:39,314
Stop fighting!

1163
01:28:59,801 --> 01:29:01,002
Let’s settle the rest later.

1164
01:29:01,336 --> 01:29:04,472
First, try my Tiger Strength tonic wine.
I oversaw its production myself.

1165
01:29:05,340 --> 01:29:08,543
Mrs. Huang, have a cup of herbal tea.

1166
01:29:08,810 --> 01:29:10,946
Thank you. Very good, very good.

1167
01:29:11,279 --> 01:29:15,283
All right, then let’s hurry
up and set the wedding date.

1168
01:29:15,684 --> 01:29:19,554
Let’s choose an auspicious day
and then have them married.

1169
01:29:19,888 --> 01:29:22,224
- All right...
- That’s right. Come on, have a drink.

1170
01:29:22,490 --> 01:29:23,959
Come on... Bottoms up!

1171
01:29:24,226 --> 01:29:26,027
Come on, cheers!

1172
01:29:46,982 --> 01:29:50,385
- You’re pulling my hair!
- Don’t pull my braid!

1173
01:29:57,592 --> 01:29:59,194
- Don’t hit me!
- I’ll hit you!

1174
01:29:59,461 --> 01:30:00,595
Let’s see if you dare hit me!

1175
01:30:00,929 --> 01:30:03,531
Mrs. Huang, you’re simply wonderful.

1176
01:30:04,933 --> 01:30:07,335
Mrs. Chen, you’re so lucky.

1177
01:30:07,669 --> 01:30:09,804
You're getting two daughters-in-law!

1178
01:30:12,207 --> 01:30:14,476
Brother Ximing, about Wuxiong...

1179
01:30:14,743 --> 01:30:17,145
I’ll go to the Liang family tomorrow
and ask for their daughter’s hand.

1180
01:30:17,412 --> 01:30:18,613
Leave it to me.

1181
01:30:18,880 --> 01:30:20,282
Tell Wuxiong not to worry.

1182
01:30:21,016 --> 01:30:22,817
Come on... Have some more wine!

1183
01:30:24,085 --> 01:30:25,353
Thank you, thank you.

1184
01:30:26,154 --> 01:30:27,756
Our big temple festival is in two days.

1185
01:30:28,089 --> 01:30:31,426
I’ll invite you all over for a little
drink at my place.

1186
01:30:31,960 --> 01:30:32,961
All right...

1187
01:30:33,628 --> 01:30:36,164
But tonight,
let’s have a proper celebration here.

1188
01:30:36,831 --> 01:30:37,032
Come!

1189
01:31:00,188 --> 01:31:02,057
Stop fighting!

1190
01:31:02,390 --> 01:31:05,860
Let’s hurry next door and see
how our parents are doing.

1191
01:31:07,062 --> 01:31:11,466
When you drink with a kindred spirit,
a thousand cups are never enough;

1192
01:31:11,800 --> 01:31:15,003
when you have nothing in common,
even half a sentence is too much.

1193
01:31:18,073 --> 01:31:22,410
All three couples should marry at once.

1194
01:31:22,677 --> 01:31:24,212
That’s right. All at once!

1195
01:31:24,546 --> 01:31:27,349
Our two families should have one
grand celebration.

1196
01:31:29,417 --> 01:31:33,221
Come to our place for the wedding
banquet the day after tomorrow.

1197
01:31:33,555 --> 01:31:36,758
Then we can each go make our preparations.

1198
01:31:37,092 --> 01:31:37,892
All right.

1199
01:31:38,159 --> 01:31:39,027
Cheers!

1200
01:31:39,894 --> 01:31:42,697
All right, come on. Cheers, cheers!

1201
01:32:10,992 --> 01:32:12,727
Dad! Mom!

1202
01:32:13,461 --> 01:32:15,063
Dad! Mom!

1203
01:32:15,330 --> 01:32:17,265
What is it? Come on, have a drink!

1204
01:32:17,532 --> 01:32:19,401
Mom, you... What happened?

1205
01:32:19,734 --> 01:32:22,137
- Mom, you’re not hurt?
- No.

1206
01:32:22,470 --> 01:32:24,873
Eldest Son, what happened to you all?

1207
01:32:25,206 --> 01:32:26,741
You’re not hurt?

1208
01:32:27,075 --> 01:32:28,410
What on earth have you been doing?

1209
01:32:28,743 --> 01:32:30,879
We were just discussing your marriages.

1210
01:32:31,212 --> 01:32:34,082
That’s right. We were discussing
your wedding arrangements.

1211
01:32:35,950 --> 01:32:38,486
You young people have such hot tempers.

1212
01:32:38,753 --> 01:32:41,156
You should drink more herbal tea.

1213
01:32:41,423 --> 01:32:44,426
That’s right, drink some herbal tea.

1214
01:32:44,826 --> 01:32:48,029
And all your marriages
have been settled quite happily.

1215
01:32:48,296 --> 01:32:49,297
Isn’t that right?

1216
01:32:50,698 --> 01:32:51,366
Yes...

1217
01:32:52,233 --> 01:32:57,038
The day after tomorrow,
everyone come to my place for the banquet.

1218
01:33:32,716 --> 01:33:34,342
Come on...

1219
01:33:35,944 --> 01:33:36,945
Cheers!

1220
01:33:37,879 --> 01:33:39,347
Come on...

1221
01:33:41,216 --> 01:33:42,417
Let me pour you a drink.

1222
01:33:42,750 --> 01:33:43,885
Come on...

1223
01:33:47,489 --> 01:33:49,691
- I’d like to offer you a toast.
- Have a little drink.

1224
01:33:52,627 --> 01:33:54,696
Come on... It’s all right, it’s all right.

1225
01:33:55,029 --> 01:33:56,831
Let’s play a finger-guessing game!

1226
01:33:57,365 --> 01:33:58,967
Come on...

1227
01:33:59,234 --> 01:34:02,504
Eight Immortals! Six in a row!

1228
01:34:02,704 --> 01:34:05,373
Here’s to our friendship!
